# Product overview

## What this is, in one sentence

A web app (mobile planned later) that pulls documents like receipts,
tickets, contracts, and statements out of a user's email — via email
forwarding or via a manual upload / drag and drop files burtton
now, and direct inbox sync in a later phase — automatically files each one
into a clear category using AI, and gives the user a searchable,
offline-capable personal document vault, so they never have to dig back
through their inbox to find an old attachment again.

## Who it's for

Individual consumers and businesses or teams. People who accumulate
important documents scattered across email: tax receipts, travel
confirmations, insurance policies, medical paperwork, subscription
confirmations, school documents. Assume non-technical users with low
tolerance for friction — onboarding, uploading, and finding a document
later should all feel close to effortless. Any UI copy, error message, or
naming decision should read naturally to that person, not to a developer.

## The core value loop

1. A document arrives — manual upload, or forwarded to the user's personal
   inbound email address.
2. It's automatically extracted, classified into a category, and summarized
   by AI.
3. The user finds it again later either by browsing categories or
   searching — in seconds, without opening their email client.
4. It stays accessible even if deleted from the original inbox, and even
   offline once the user explicitly saves it for offline access.

## Feature set

### Being built now — this build (v1)

- Manual upload via a button and drag-and-drop
- A unique per-user inbound email address for forwarding documents in, created when new user signs up
- AI classification into a category, plus a short AI-generated summary of
  the source email/document
- Dashboard: category grid → category document list → document viewer with AI summary of the document beside opened document
- Full-text search across summaries and filenames
- Offline access to individually-saved documents (installable PWA)
- Stripe subscription billing (Free / Pro / Business, gated on storage)
- Account settings: view/regenerate inbound address, manage billing

### Deliberately deferred — not forgotten, not to be built into this phase

- Automatic Gmail/Outlook inbox scanning. This requires Google's CASA
  third-party security assessment before it can be offered beyond ~100 test
  users — a sequencing decision, not an oversight. Do not build OAuth
  mailbox-reading scopes, or a `connected_mail_accounts`-style table, into
  the current build unless a phase prompt explicitly asks for it.
- iOS and Android native apps. Planned as React Native + Expo, sharing
  types and API client code with the web app via the monorepo — this is
  *why* business logic belongs in the backend/worker and shared packages
  rather than directly in Next.js components, even at v1.
- Push-based (real-time) mailbox sync.
- Multi-category tagging — v1 is one primary category per document.
- Cloud OCR/document-AI upgrade for scanned images — v1 uses free,
  self-hosted Tesseract.

### Explicitly out of scope, not planned

- Team or multi-user shared accounts.
- Editing document contents within the app — it's a vault, not an editor.

## Category taxonomy

Seeded per user at signup, user-editable afterward: Receipts & Purchases,
Travel & Tickets, Bills & Utilities, Subscriptions & Memberships, Work &
Business, School & Education, Insurance, Taxes & Finance, Medical & Health,
Legal & Contracts, Identification & Personal Docs, and the permanent system
category Needs Review, where low-AI-confidence results land instead of
being silently misfiled.

## Tech stack, by component

| Component | Choice |
|---|---|
| Web app | Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS |
| Background worker | Standalone Node.js + TypeScript service — not a serverless function |
| Database & auth | Supabase (PostgreSQL + Row Level Security + Supabase Auth) |
| File storage | Cloudflare R2, envelope-encrypted at rest |
| Inbound email parsing | Cloudflare Email Routing + a Cloudflare Worker |
| AI classification | OpenAI API, structured JSON outputs |
| Job queue | Upstash Redis + BullMQ |
| Payments | Stripe (Checkout, Customer Portal, webhooks) |
| Error monitoring | Sentry |
| Web hosting | Vercel |
| Worker hosting | Fly.io or Railway |
| Monorepo tooling | Turborepo |
| Future mobile | React Native + Expo, sharing types/API client with web |

## Business model

Freemium subscription via Stripe. The free tier ships with the app from
day one; Pro and Business unlock more storage. The real variable cost
driver is AI processing per document, not raw storage — pricing may evolve
to reflect that later, but v1 gates on storage since it's the simplest
thing to explain to a non-technical user.

## How to use this when working on any single phase

Every phase in this build is one piece of the loop described above. When a
phase's literal instructions are ambiguous or silent on something, resolve
it in the direction that serves this whole product, not just the narrowest
reading of that one phase's prompt — and if a phase prompt seems to
conflict with something in this file (for example, asking you to build
something listed above as deliberately deferred), say so explicitly rather
than proceeding either way silently.
